    {
      "id": "I_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABQKgkPQ",
      "title": "zk: Align ZK dispute game terminology with the interop dependency set",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 940,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "body": "**Claude:**\n\nThe ZK dispute game pages use two terms for the set of chains that a super root commits to. Neither term matches the one the interop pages use.\n\nThe interop pages call this the [dependency set](https://specs.optimism.io/interop/dependency-set.html). The ZK pages call it the \"chain set\" and the \"interop set\", sometimes in the same sentence.\n\n`specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-dispute-game.md` defines \"Chain Set\" as its own term:\n\n```\n### Chain Set\n\nThe set of chains whose output roots are committed to by a super root. Defined by the\n`SuperRootProof` preimage in `extraData`. In a standalone deployment the chain set contains\nexactly one chain.\n```\n\nTwo assumptions are named after it: `aZKG-008: Super Root Preimage Faithfully Represents the Chain Set` and `aZKG-009: Chain Set Is Stable During the Prove Window`.\n\n\"Interop set\" is also used where the set can hold a single chain, which reads as a contradiction:\n\n- `specs/fault-proof/zk-fault-proof-vm.md`: \"In a standalone deployment (single chain), the interop set contains exactly one chain.\"\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-interface.md`: \"cover every chain in the interop set (or a single entry in standalone deployments)\"\n\nAffected files:\n\n- `specs/fault-proof/zk-fault-proof-vm.md`\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-dispute-game.md`\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-interface.md`\n- `specs/fault-proof/stage-one/zk/zk-migration.md`\n\nSuggested fix: use \"dependency set\" everywhere, and state that the dependency set may contain a single chain. This removes the need for a separate standalone term. Renaming the two assumptions changes their headings, so the anchors change.\n\nContext: ethereum-optimism/specs#939 removed a \"Chain Set\" section from the super root dispute game page for this reason, and uses \"dependency set\" instead.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-07T22:55:53Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 0
    }
  ],
